docs {
  Executes a read-only (constant) smart-contract call — no transaction is
  created and no energy is consumed.

  The example calls `balanceOf(address)` on the USDT (TRC20) contract:
  `data` = base64 of the ABI-encoded call (selector `70a08231` + padded address).

  **Service:** `protocol.Wallet` · **Method:** `TriggerConstantContract` (unary)

  All `bytes` fields are sent as **base64 of the raw bytes** (protobuf JSON mapping).
  For a TRON address, base58-decode it (or take the 21-byte hex form starting with `41`)
  and base64-encode the raw bytes, e.g. `echo 41E552...32CD0 | xxd -r -p | base64`.
}
